    "recommendations": "• Mark each building with clearly visible address numbers on all sides facing access roads or parking areas.\n\n• Mark the primary and secondary access points with reflective signage to help responders identify entry routes quickly, especially at night.\n\n• Keep the internal drive aisle clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and stored materials to allow emergency vehicles to move between structures.\n\n• Post visible directional signage along the internal drive aisle identifying each building by name or number.\n\n• Keep the loading area clear of trailers, pallets, and equipment when not in active use so emergency vehicles can stage or reposition.\n\n• Mark a designated staging area for emergency vehicles that does not block the internal drive aisle or loading area access.\n\n• Keep outdoor storage and material storage areas organized so that clear walking paths exist around the perimeter of each storage zone.\n\n• Keep dumpster enclosure gates fully closeable and verify that the enclosure does not obstruct vehicle movement along the drive aisle.\n\n• Mark the rear access route with signage indicating its availability and any weight or clearance restrictions visible along that path.\n\n• Identify and mark the limited rear access point so responding crews are aware of the access constraint before committing vehicles to that route."
